# What `just web` copies from generated/ into dist/generated/: the baked files
# Bevy loads over HTTP (buildings, props, texture maps, pictures, material
# libraries). Layouts and registries ride in data.bundle.gz, and so do the rivers' index
# and the masses within 96 km of the spawn. The farther masses reach
# dist/generated/hydrology/mass because `xtask bundle` writes them beside its
# output (run after `rm -rf dist`, before an rsync that deletes nothing).
# The rest (the capacity bench, the
# material graphs, the statistics) is read by no one in a browser.
- /capacity/
- /hydrology/
- /stats/
- /materials/capacity/
# The terrain's layer maps are read only to pack the arrays on the CPU for a
# look that asks for another cavity shade than the baked one; the page ships
# the baked arrays (terrain/*.ktx2) and the default look.
- /materials/terrain/
- graphs.ron
+ */
+ *.ashlar
+ *.ashprop
+ *.ktx2
+ *.png
+ *.materials.ron
- *
